{"name":"FantasY2K","title":"FantasY2K","revision":231188,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/FantasY2K","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The aesthetic takes an unapologetically kitsch approach in its disregard for historical accuracy in favor of contemporary trends. For this reason, it is often adopted with self-aware irony, particularly in satirical media such as A Knight's Tale or Ella Enchanted."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"FantasY2K is very distinct from other fantasy inspired aesthetics such as Fairy Grunge and Mythpunk, due to its far brighter colour palette and its whimsical, often camp, sensibilities. Although it shares some motifs with Fairycore, it is differentiated by its more direct appropriation of Y2K aesthetics and a more significant Medieval influence."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Common visual motifs include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Highly-Saturated Color Palettes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Poorly-Rendered Digital Artwork"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gaudy/Cluttered Compositions"},{"kind":"list","text":"Highly-Stylized Landscapes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Overly-Edited Photographs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Luminescent or Holographic Effects"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Clothing elements and motifs include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Velvet"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brocade"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crochet"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lace"},{"kind":"list","text":"Silk"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chiffon"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lace-up Details"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corsets/Stays"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long Skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hip Belts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flare Sleeves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Puff Sleeves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Empire Waistlines"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dropped Waistlines"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metallic Beading"},{"kind":"list","text":"Embroidery"},{"kind":"list","text":"Art Nouveau Motifs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bohemian Influences"},{"kind":"list","text":"Elaborate Jewellery"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ever After (1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Knight in Camelot (1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Midsummer Night’s Dream (1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The 10th Kingdom (2000)"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Knight's Tale (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black Knight (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shrek franchise (2001-)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Mists of Avalon (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Big Fish (2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ella Enchanted (2004)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Once Upon a Mattress (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stardust (2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Enchanted (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Virgin Territory (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rosaline (2022)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"TV Shows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Buffy the Vampire Slayer (1997-2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Charmed (1998 - 2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Fairly OddParents (2001-2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Winx Club (2004-2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Robin Hood (2006-2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Power Rangers: Mystic Force (2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Merlin (2008-2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Legend of the Seeker (2008-2010)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Articles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fashion's Going Medieval - i.D. Vice"},{"kind":"list","text":"Middle Ages Modern is a New Aesthetic for Our Increasingly Medieval Times - Architectural Digest"},{"kind":"list","text":"What is EnyaCore? Meet the Moody, Medieval Side of the Next Y2K Aesthetic - Vice"},{"kind":"list","text":"Why the Medieval Aesthetic Never Dies: The History of Medieval Revival Fashion (video essay) - Kaz Rowe"},{"kind":"list","text":"FAIRYTALE COSTUMES: it's giving renfaire but why? (video essay) - Mina Lee"}],"contentStat